 "description": "Search for places (cities, towns, landmarks, regions) by name and get which STATE / PROVINCE / COUNTY / PREFECTURE / administrative division (German Bundesland, UK county, Canadian province, Japanese prefecture, Indian/Australian/Mexican state, etc.) they are in, plus country, coordinates, population, and feature type. Answers \"what state is <city> in\", \"which US/German/Australian state is <city> in\", \"what province/county/prefecture/region is <place> in\" \u2014 the `admin_region` field is the state/province/county/prefecture (e.g. search_geonames(\"Naperville\", \"US\") \u2192 Illinois; (\"Heidelberg\", \"DE\") \u2192 Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg; (\"Leeds\", \"GB\") \u2192 England; (\"Osaka\", \"JP\") \u2192 Osaka). Worldwide coverage. Example: search_geonames(\"Paris\", \"FR\"). Use get_nearby to find places near a known location.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "examples": [
   {
    "query": "Tokyo"
   },
   {
    "country": "US",
    "limit": 5,
    "query": "Grand Canyon"
   }
  ],
  "properties": {
   "_apiKey": {
    "description": "GeoNames username",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "country": {
    "description": "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code to filter (e.g., \"US\", \"JP\")",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "limit": {
    "description": "Number of results (default: 10, max: 100)",
    "type": "number"
   },
   "query": {
    "description": "Place name to search for (e.g., \"Tokyo\", \"Grand Canyon\")",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
